      "created_at": "2026-07-21T04:18:33Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-07-21T04:18:33Z",
      "body": "`__next__` is supposed to be called immediately after `__iter__`, in the same thread, of course.\r\n\r\n```\r\ndef f(x: *tuple[int]):\r\n```\r\n\r\nSo there should not be any race condition on practice. I do not mind using atomic exchange here, but I think that such large and expensive test is not worth it. Remove it.",
      "author_association": "MEMBER",
